WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.482
Investigation

00:00:01.553 --> 00:00:02.236
Novita

00:00:02.319 --> 00:00:03.533
StreamLake and Ant

00:00:03.345 --> 00:00:04.689
Digital route OpenRouter

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:05.609
model requests

00:00:06.126 --> 00:00:07.824
A data-driven investigation

00:00:07.635 --> 00:00:08.708
finds fingerprints

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.052
showing several OpenRouter

00:00:09.864 --> 00:00:11.031
inference providers

00:00:11.185 --> 00:00:12.541
including ones marketed

00:00:12.364 --> 00:00:13.366
as zero data

00:00:13.178 --> 00:00:13.932
retention

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:15.371
forward DeepSeek

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:17.148
The evidence includes

00:00:17.007 --> 00:00:18.303
image downloads from

00:00:18.115 --> 00:00:19.577
ByteDance cloud IP

00:00:19.389 --> 00:00:20.049
ranges

00:00:20.202 --> 00:00:21.935
ByteDance-format upstream

00:00:21.747 --> 00:00:23.068
request IDs and

00:00:22.962 --> 00:00:24.152
Ark-style tool-call

00:00:23.964 --> 00:00:24.707
IDs

00:00:24.919 --> 00:00:26.287
gateway error messages

00:00:26.099 --> 00:00:27.159
copied word for

00:00:26.971 --> 00:00:28.516
word between providers

00:00:29.054 --> 00:00:30.044
The author notes

00:00:29.856 --> 00:00:31.671
Novita sent 120

00:00:31.483 --> 00:00:33.216
to 160 billion

00:00:33.028 --> 00:00:33.959
tokens a day

00:00:33.771 --> 00:00:34.737
on these models

00:00:34.549 --> 00:00:35.752
until OpenRouter

00:00:35.858 --> 00:00:37.249
removed its ZDR

00:00:37.061 --> 00:00:38.700
label on November 20

00:00:38.783 --> 00:00:39.643
and that routes

00:00:39.455 --> 00:00:40.362
keep shifting

00:00:40.902 --> 00:00:41.916
Full story on

00:00:41.727 --> 00:00:42.623
the dashboard
